# 20 -- Serial ports
#
# Only ports whose PROTOCOL or BAUD differ from the TBS_LUCID_H7 board defaults
# are listed. Wiring is in ardupilot.md "Serial ports" and flight-platform.md.
# BAUD is in kbaud (115 = 115200, 460 = 460800, 1500 = 1.5 Mbaud).
#
# SERIAL2 -- Holybro F9P Rover Lite: sole GNSS on the mast (UART + I2C compass),
#   the old M100 port. GPS1_COM_PORT follows this UART. RTCM/RTK corrections are
#   forwarded to the F9P here. Proto 5 = GPS.
#   [ardupilot.md; rtk-corrections-path.md]  provenance: 4f82b3d 2026-06-21
SERIAL2_PROTOCOL,5
SERIAL2_BAUD,115
#
# SERIAL3 -- Walksnail VTX MSP DisplayPort (TX3/RX3 only; VTX power is on other
#   FC pads, not this UART). Proto 42 = MSP DisplayPort. Board-default baud.
SERIAL3_PROTOCOL,42
SERIAL3_BAUD,115
#
# SERIAL4 -- Coordinator (Pi 4B, VIO) companion link. Proto 2 = MAVLink2, which
#   ExtNav/VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE ingest requires. 1.5 Mbaud is the measured
#   working rate for the VIO stream (raised from 460 on 2026-07-08).
#   [ardupilot.md; docs/vio-integration.md]  provenance: 04b2592, bcd7c65 2026-07-08
SERIAL4_PROTOCOL,2
SERIAL4_BAUD,1500
#
# SERIAL6 -- Matek ELRS R24-TD. Proto 2 = MAVLink2 (control + telemetry + the
#   RTCM uplink path). 460800 must match the ELRS link rate. Board default here
#   is proto 23 (RCIN); we drive full MAVLink instead.
#   [ground-station.md; rtk-corrections-path.md]
SERIAL6_PROTOCOL,2
SERIAL6_BAUD,460
#
# SERIAL7 -- Unused. Board default is proto 2; we disable it. (An earlier plan to
#   move the F9P here was abandoned; F9P stayed on SERIAL2.)
#   provenance: 4f82b3d 2026-06-21
SERIAL7_PROTOCOL,-1
SERIAL7_BAUD,115
#
# SERIAL8 -- ESC telemetry ribbon (AM32 4in1). Proto 16 = ESC telemetry; feeds
#   motor RPM to the harmonic notch (see 50-esc-motors-notch) and volts/amps to
#   BATT_MONITOR=9 (see 70-battery). This is the board default protocol; baud
#   differs (115 vs board 57).  [ardupilot.md ESC section]
SERIAL8_BAUD,115
#
# SERIAL9 -- OTG serial, listed unused. Proto 2, baud raised to 460 on
#   2026-06-28 ("if it matters"). provenance: 23a5591
SERIAL9_PROTOCOL,2
SERIAL9_BAUD,460
#
# Note: SERIAL0 (USB console, proto 2 / 115) and SERIAL1 (unused, proto -1) sit
# at board defaults and are intentionally omitted here.
